  "positive_findings": [
    "The strict hard-categorical no-bypass architecture was implemented and independently inspected.",
    "The answer path was architecturally restricted to predicted hard z2, predicted hard z3, and the answer decoder.",
    "True z2 and z3 labels were training targets and were not consumed downstream at inference.",
    "The retained scored hard categories were the exact categories consumed by the transition and answer modules.",
    "Models 1 and 3 passed every frozen protected qualification gate.",
    "Model 2 passed all aggregate answer, z2, and z3 gates but failed one registered powered subgroup gate.",
    "The result validly establishes seed heterogeneity under the frozen architecture, recipe, checkpoints, and qualification population."
  ],
  "strongest_safe_claim": "The strict no-bypass supervised bottleneck architecture was feasible in multiple frozen seeds, but the frozen architecture and training recipe did not satisfy the preregistered three-of-three robustness requirement across these three seeds.",
